eurological deficit is absent", "Hypertensive encephalopathy: No evidence of acute blood pressure fluctuation to support this mechanism"], "alarm_features": ["Severe altered mental status (GCS 7)", "Post-traumatic deterioration"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Traumatic Intracranial Hemorrhage", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.8404669260700388, "posterior": 0.3986897519887693, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Uncharacterized head CT abnormalities are common in traumatic cases and often show convexity/subdural features consistent with B1. The absence of definitive imaging characteristics prevents strong assignment.", "Brief post-traumatic unconsciousness and functional recovery patterns distinguish traumatic injuries from acute strokes (typically prolonged unconsciousness and static neurological deficits). This strengthens trauma-related mechanisms."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3", "B1.4"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Presence of basilar skull fracture signs (e.g. Battle's sign, raccoon eyes)", "Location and pattern of CT abnormality (convexity vs. infratentorial vs. focal)"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Head CT characteristics (location, size, associated midline shift)", "Lumbar puncture to detect subarachnoid hemorrhage (if CT-negative after 48 hours)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.95, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Non-Traumatic Cerebrovascular Event", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.0584932147870847, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Brief post-traumatic unconsciousness and functional recovery patterns distinguish traumatic injuries from acute strokes (typically prolonged unconsciousness and static neurological deficits). This strengthens trauma-related mechanisms."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Post-Traumatic Cerebral Vasospasm", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.023397285914833883, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Post-Traumatic Cerebral Edema", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.014038371548900327, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Acute Traumatic Subdural Hemorrhage (Cerebral Bridging Vein Injury)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.22461394478240526, "danger": 0.95, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of Battle's sign and ability to ski argue against basilar skull fracture-induced subarachnoid hemorrhage."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Traumatic Epidural Hemorrhage (Middle Meningeal Artery Injury)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.07019185774450164, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Gradual GCS decline provides strong evidence against epidural hemorrhage from middle meningeal artery injury."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Cerebral Parenchymal Hemorrhage/Contusion (Traumatic Brain Injury)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.0898455779129621, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Skiing ability does not strongly support severe cerebral contusion but provides moderate reduction in likelihood."]}, "B1.4": {"id": "B1.4", "label": "Traumatic Subarachnoid Hemorrhage (Basilar Skull Fracture)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.014038371548900329, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of Battle's sign and ability to ski argue against basilar skull fracture-induced subarachnoid hemorrhage."]}}, "frontier": [], "other_